This unexpected result makes me suspect a fundamental misunderstanding on my part or, perhaps, a highly unusual project configuration. I know that `spring-boot-dependencies` is indeed a 
BOM, and its primary role is to *import* other BOMs and define versions for commonly used dependencies. However, it doesn't necessarily mean that *every* `spring-boot-starter-*` artifact 
will be directly listed in its own `dependencyManagement` section. Typically, the `spring-boot-starter-*` modules themselves are not POMs in the Maven Central repository; they are JARs 
that, in turn, depend on other modules.

